{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.modulusReading_gives_pythagorean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.modulusReading_gives_pythagorean","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L146-L155","doc":"**Conditional derivation (sorry-free).** *Given* the modulus-reading hypothesis, the A=3\nmagnitude is the Pythagorean quadrature of the (derived, bar-even) self-adjoint reduction and\nthe transverse slope: `r*² = fs² + s²`. No instance of the hypothesis is constructed — the\nmodulus reading and the `|χ| = 1` input are the open premises (beans `qou-wiub`/`qou-wgnx`),\nso this is a genuine *conditional* result, never a closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.physical_modulus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.physical_modulus","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L144-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.carrier_unitModulus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.carrier_unitModulus","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L143-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.carrier_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.carrier_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L142-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.bar_even_s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.bar_even_s","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L141-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.bar_even_fs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.bar_even_fs","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L140-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.rStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.rStar","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.E","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.E","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L138-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.s","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L137-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.fs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.fs","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L136-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.σ","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L135-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L134-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.ModulusReadingHypothesis","kind":"structure","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L126-L144","doc":"**The modulus-reading hypothesis (content-bearing; NO instance is constructed).** Bundles\nthe derived inputs — a bar-involution `σ`, the bar-even self-adjoint reduction `fs`, the\nbar-even transverse slope `s`, the bar-odd unit-modulus carrier `E`, and the target `rStar` —\ntogether with the *physical modulus reading* `rStar² = factor_ℂ · σ(factor_ℂ)` (that the\nphysical A=3 lift is the modulus of the complex affine carrier). This is the OPEN premise\n(§3b): it is **not** inhabited here — an inhabitant needs a ring hosting `√−1` with a genuine\ninvolution *and* the branching-derived `fs, s` making the reading hold; constructing one to\nhit `rStar = 1.585` would be the forbidden fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.sq_ne_neg_one_of_ordered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.sq_ne_neg_one_of_ordered","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L112-L122","doc":"**The carrier is not real (sorry-free).** In any ordered field, `E² = −1` is impossible\n(`E² ≥ 0 > −1`). With Part 1 this is the exact statement of the \"real `E` vs complex phase\"\ntype tension: the bar-odd unit-modulus carrier `E = χ(P)` **cannot** live in the real ordered\nlift field of `A3AntiSelfAdjointLift` — it is genuinely transverse (imaginary-`q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.barOdd_carrier_quadrature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.barOdd_carrier_quadrature","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L100-L108","doc":"**The bridge (sorry-free).** Bar-even background `(fs, s)`, bar-odd (`σ E = −E`)\nunit-modulus (`E · σ E = 1`) carrier `E` ⇒ the affine lift's modulus is `fs² + s²`. Combines\nParts 1–2: the unit-modulus phase supplies a **real** magnitude to the lift via quadrature. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.affine_modulus_quadrature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.affine_modulus_quadrature","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L88-L98","doc":"**Quadrature identity (sorry-free).** For a ring-hom bar involution `σ : K →+* K`, a\nbar-even self-adjoint reduction `fs` (`σ fs = fs`), a bar-even slope `s` (`σ s = s`), and a\nbar-odd carrier `E` (`σ E = −E`) with `E² = −1`, the \"modulus\" `factor_ℂ · σ(factor_ℂ)` of the\naffine lift `factor_ℂ = fs − s·E` is the **sum of squares** `fs² + s²` — the `−s²E²` cross-term\nbecomes `+s²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.barOdd_unitModulus_sq_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.barOdd_unitModulus_sq_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffBarOddPythagorasBridge.lean#L75-L84","doc":"**Bar-odd + unit-modulus ⇒ `E² = −1` (sorry-free).** For a carrier `E` in any commutative\nring with a bar involution `σ`, if `E` is bar-odd (`σ E = −E`, anti-self-adjoint) and has unit\nmodulus (`E · σ E = 1`, the `|χ| = 1` datum), then `E` is a square root of `−1`. This is the\nalgebraic core of the \"real amplitude vs unit phase\" type tension: the carrier is genuinely\n`√−1`, never a real scalar. ","signatureChunk":0}]}